## 16. Comprehensive Failure-Mode Analysis & Error Handling

To ensure high reliability on production edge clusters and embedded robotics systems, the scheduler implements a strict **no-silent-failures** policy with a structured domain exception hierarchy.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class GPUSchedulerError {
        <<Base Exception>>
    }
    class InvalidTenantConfigError
    class InvalidQuantumError
    class InvalidExecutionTimeError
    class EmptyQueueError
    class TenantQuotaExhaustedError
    class SchedulerStarvationError
    class PredictorUnavailableError
    class InvalidPredictorOutputError
    class ModelNotFoundError
    class ConfigurationCorruptedError
    class CUDAUnavailableError
    class TensorRTUnavailableError
    class GPUMemoryAllocationError
    class HardwareExecutionError
    class JobCancelledError
    class DuplicateJobError
    class UnknownTenantError

    GPUSchedulerError <|-- InvalidTenantConfigError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- InvalidQuantumError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- InvalidExecutionTimeError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- EmptyQueueError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- TenantQuotaExhaustedError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- SchedulerStarvationError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- PredictorUnavailableError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- InvalidPredictorOutputError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- ModelNotFoundError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- ConfigurationCorruptedError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- CUDAUnavailableError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- TensorRTUnavailableError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- GPUMemoryAllocationError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- HardwareExecutionError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- JobCancelledError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- DuplicateJobError
    GPUSchedulerError <|-- UnknownTenantError
```

### Handled Failure Modes & Mitigations

| # | Failure Mode | Trigger / Condition | Exception / Handling Mechanism | Safety Guarantee |
|---|--------------|---------------------|--------------------------------|------------------|
| **1** | **Invalid Tenant Configuration** | Negative weights, priority $\notin [1, 10]$, quota $\le 0$ or $> 100\%$, NaN/Inf weights, empty string IDs. | Raises `InvalidTenantConfigError` (subclass of `ValueError`). | Rejection at configuration initialization; avoids divide-by-zero or scheduling loops. |
| **2** | **Invalid GPU Quantum** | $Q_{\text{base}} \le 0$, $Q_{\text{min}} > Q_{\text{base}}$, or $Q_{\text{base}} > Q_{\text{max}}$. | Raises `InvalidQuantumError` (subclass of `ValueError`) across scheduler config, simulator, and executors. | Guarantees well-ordered, strictly positive time slicing intervals. |
| **3** | **Zero GPU Execution Time** | $T_{\text{exec}} \le 0$ requested for submission or slice execution. | Raises `InvalidExecutionTimeError` (subclass of `ValueError`) in simulator & executors. | Prevents infinite zero-work dispatch loops and zero-duration trace spikes. |
| **4** | **Negative Execution Time** | Negative remaining runtime or negative slice duration. | Raises `InvalidExecutionTimeError` in `GPUJob` constructor, `execute_slice()`, and simulator. | Preserves monotonicity of remaining job runtimes and timestamps. |
| **5** | **Empty Queues** | No eligible jobs waiting in queues during scheduling pass. | All schedulers return `None` safely. Strict queue consumers call `dequeue_strict()` raising `EmptyQueueError`. | Safe simulator idle progression; no crashes or `IndexError` on zero-backlog states. |
| **6** | **Tenant Quota Exhaustion** | Tenant exceeds sliding-window GPU allocation limit. | Fair scheduler throttles tenant by skipping queue. `Tenant.enforce_quota_strict()` raises `TenantQuotaExhaustedError`. | Prevents noisy tenants from exceeding reserved GPU capacity without hanging simulator. |
| **7** | **Scheduler Starvation** | Waiting job delayed beyond $T_{\text{starve}} = 2000\,\text{ms}$. | Warning logged with detailed telemetry. `check_starvation_violations(strict=True)` raises `SchedulerStarvationError`. | Aging term dynamically raises score; strict mode asserts anti-starvation invariants. |
| **8** | **Predictor Unavailable** | Model file missing or model not trained. | Non-strict mode: logs warning and transparently falls back to heuristic baseline. `predict_strict()` raises `PredictorUnavailableError`. | Scheduling pipeline continues seamlessly with zero downtime when ML fails. |
| **9** | **Predictor Returns Invalid Output** | ML inference returns NaN, Inf, negative latency, or out-of-range confidence scores. | `PredictionOutput` validation and scheduler sanitization raise `InvalidPredictorOutputError` or clamp to heuristic defaults. | ML inference corruption cannot inject NaN or infinite scores into scheduling calculations. |
| **10** | **Missing ML Model** | Specified `.joblib` file does not exist or has corrupted pickle bytes. | `LightweightWorkloadPredictor.load()` raises `ModelNotFoundError` (subclass of `FileNotFoundError`). | Clear error message pointing to missing path; no silent `NoneType` bugs. |
| **11** | **Corrupted Experiment Config** | Malformed YAML syntax or missing root schema keys (`tenants`, `workload`, etc.). | `load_*_config()` raises `ConfigurationCorruptedError` with underlying parsing details. | Halts invalid benchmarking runs early before partial experiment corruption occurs. |
| **12** | **CUDA Unavailable** | Hardware dispatch attempted on a non-CUDA host (e.g., macOS dev laptop). | `JetsonExecutor.dispatch_slice()` raises `CUDAUnavailableError`. `create_executor(backend="jetson", strict=False)` safely falls back to `SimulationExecutor`. | Cross-platform portability: runs simulations on laptops while supporting strict checks on Jetson. |
| **13** | **TensorRT Unavailable** | Jetson executor requests TRT optimization but `tensorrt` is not installed. | `JetsonExecutor.enable_tensorrt(strict=True)` raises `TensorRTUnavailableError`. Non-strict returns `False` and uses PyTorch. | Eliminates silent missing-dependency issues during deployment. |
| **14** | **GPU Memory Allocation Failure** | Model weights and batch size exceed total device VRAM capacity. | Catches host/device OOM and memory limits, raising `GPUMemoryAllocationError` (subclass of `MemoryError`). | Prevents silent process crashes; allows upper orchestration layer to reschedule or throttle. |
| **15** | **Hardware Executor Failure** | CUDA kernel launch error, stream synchronization error, or device driver failure. | Wraps unhandled hardware runtime exceptions into `HardwareExecutionError`. | Structured error context containing tensor shape, model name, and kernel traceback. |
| **16** | **Job Cancellation** | Job cancelled by user/client while in queue or during execution. | Transitioned to `JobState.CANCELLED`. Attempting to start or execute raises `JobCancelledError`. | Job removed from active queues; GPU resource freed immediately without zombie execution. |
| **17** | **Duplicate Job IDs** | Job submitted with an ID that already exists in the queue or simulator. | `TenantJobQueue.enqueue()` and `GPUSimulator.submit_job()` raise `DuplicateJobError`. | Guarantees uniqueness of job telemetry, traces, and metrics. |
| **18** | **Unknown Tenant IDs** | Job references a tenant not registered in `TenantQueueManager` or `GPUFairScheduler`. | Raises `UnknownTenantError` (subclass of `KeyError`). | Prevents orphaned jobs from executing without tenant accounting or quota tracking. |
